      "problem": "Evaluate $f(2,1)$ if $f(x,y)=(x-3y)(x+y)^{2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We substitute $x=2$ and $y=1$ into the function definition and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =(x-3y)(x+y)^{2} \\\\ f(2,1) & =(2-3(1))(2+1)^{2} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (3)^{2} \\\\  & =-1\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
